- op: discuss  # 92b9
  at: '2026-10-25T03:44:06Z'  # 92b9
  by: agent  # 92b9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 92b9
  clock: 3  # 92b9
  nonce: 92b9  # 92b9
  message: "Fixed in PR #1842 (dev f040f5649d). The PR also carries 2e24237a46, which moves WI-mifag's typed_references onto the inheritance-family registry; the live-tree linter had caught it.\n\nThe fix: TreeSitterAnalyzer.grammar_distribution() names the PyPI distribution from the class's grammar_module (underscores become hyphens, checked against packages_distributions) or language_pack_name. The catalog publishes it whenever the registry gives no `requires`: 45 passes now name a dedicated wheel and 60 the language pack. Before, all 63 _ts() passes said language pack, and 42 others said nothing. is_available() now requires the base library AND the named distribution's module.\n\nLive repro on merged dev:\n- get_default_catalog(): rust requires \"tree-sitter-rust\" (was \"tree-sitter-language-pack\"); csharp \"tree-sitter-c-sharp\"; apex \"tree-sitter-language-pack\".\n- `hypergumbo catalog` (through main) with importlib.util.find_spec patched to hide tree_sitter_rust: \"rust (extra): Rust via tree-sitter [not installed]\", go unaffected. Unpatched: no marker. Before the fix, the substring test reported rust available in that state.\n\nCorrection to the item's description: the CLI text and JSON views do not print `requires`. Users see it through is_available's \"[not installed]\" marker and the JSON `available` flag; Catalog.to_dict carries the field itself.\n\nNOT done: no bare venv was rebuilt to re-run ADR-0056's acceptance test with the language pack uninstalled."  # 92b9
